.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B class pyotp.totp.TOTP(s: str \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:stdtypes\:.html#\:str>, digits: int \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:int> = 6, digest: Any \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:typing\:.html#\:typing\:.Any> = None, name: str \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:stdtypes\:.html#\:str> | None \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:constants\:.html#\:None> = None, issuer: str \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:stdtypes\:.html#\:str> | None \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:constants\:.html#\:None> = None, interval: int \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:int> = 30)
Handler for time\-based OTP counters.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B at(for_time: int \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:int> | datetime \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:datetime\:.html#\:datetime\:.datetime>, counter_offset: int \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:int> = 0) -> str \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:stdtypes\:.html#\:str>
Accepts either a Unix timestamp integer or a datetime object.
.sp
To get the time until the next timecode change (seconds until the current OTP expires), use this instead:
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
totp = pyotp.TOTP(...)
time_remaining = totp.interval \- datetime.datetime.now().timestamp() % totp.interval
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Parameters
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfor_time\fP \-\- the time to generate an OTP for
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcounter_offset\fP \-\- the amount of ticks to add to the time counter
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B Returns
OTP value
