Returns the provisioning URI for the OTP; works for either TOTP or HOTP.
.sp
This can then be encoded in a QR Code and used to provision the Google
Authenticator app.
.sp
For module\-internal use.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B See also:
\%<https://\:github\:.com/\:google/\:google-authenticator/\:wiki/\:Key-Uri-Format>
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Parameters
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsecret\fP \-\- the hotp/totp secret used to generate the URI
.IP \(bu 2
\fBname\fP \-\- name of the account
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinitial_count\fP \-\- starting counter value, defaults to None.
If none, the OTP type will be assumed as TOTP.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBissuer\fP \-\- the name of the OTP issuer; this will be the
organization title of the OTP entry in Authenticator
.IP \(bu 2
\fBalgorithm\fP \-\- the algorithm used in the OTP generation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdigits\fP \-\- the length of the OTP generated code.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBperiod\fP \-\- the number of seconds the OTP generator is set to
expire every code.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBkwargs\fP \-\- other query string parameters to include in the URI
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B Returns
provisioning uri
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B pyotp.utils.strings_equal(s1: str \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:stdtypes\:.html#\:str>, s2: str \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:stdtypes\:.html#\:str>) -> bool \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:bool>
Timing\-attack resistant string comparison.
.sp
Normal comparison using == will short\-circuit on the first mismatching
character. This avoids that by scanning the whole string, though we
still reveal to a timing attack whether the strings are the same
length.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B class pyotp.contrib.steam.Steam(s: str \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:stdtypes\:.html#\:str>, name: str \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:stdtypes\:.html#\:str> | None \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:constants\:.html#\:None> = None, issuer: str \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:stdtypes\:.html#\:str> | None \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:constants\:.html#\:None> = None, interval: int \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:int> = 30, digits: int \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:int> = 5)
Steam\(aqs custom TOTP. Subclass of \fIpyotp.totp.TOTP\fP\&.
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B generate_otp(input: int \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:int>) -> str \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:stdtypes\:.html#\:str>
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Parameters
\fBinput\fP \-\- the HMAC counter value to use as the OTP input.
Usually either the counter, or the computed integer based on the Unix timestamp
